#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
dispatch-advise: advisory agent + skill router (D0-2 of v11-leverage-program, ticket #88).

Ranks the live roster (scripts/lib/roster.py) against a task and prints the
top-3 agents, the top-3 skills and a derived complexity / model tier / effort.
It never writes the orchestrator's metadata.agent / scope, is never called from
a hook, and puts nothing anywhere but stdout and the side log.

Usage:
    scripts/dispatch-advise --text "add an nginx site for foo" [--json] [--no-log]
    scripts/dispatch-advise --task-id 20 --project v11-leverage-program [--json]
                            [--session UUID] [--epoch TL_EPOCH]
    scripts/dispatch-advise --pending v11-leverage-program [--json] [--no-log]
    scripts/dispatch-advise --engine baseline ...      # default (and only) engine
    scripts/dispatch-advise ... --no-prior --no-tiebreak  # engine relevance alone

Pipeline per task (fixed routes first, then the engine, then shared post-steps):
  1. Fixed routes short-circuit agent scoring, in this order. route.provenance
     records where the route came from (review_of | subject | description |
     engine), and every advice carries brief_has_pasted_text (a ``` fence, a >
     quote line, or a double-quoted span of PASTED_QUOTE_MIN_CHARS+), so a
     consumer can refuse to auto-apply a route read out of pasted material.
       fixer           metadata.review_of + a fix marker (metadata.fix truthy,
                       metadata.kind/type in FIX_KINDS, or a subject that opens
                       with "Fix") -> adversarial-lite-fixer         [review_of]
       review_sibling  metadata.review_of -> adversarial-lite-reviewer [review_of]
       explicit_agent  the subject (or --text) instructs a roster agent:
                       "use X", "delegate to X", "agent=X", "@X"; the weak
                       verbs using/via/let/have need "X agent".        [subject]
       review_text     a subject opening "Review: ..." / "review task #7"
                       -> adversarial-lite-reviewer                    [subject]
       explicit_agent  the description's FIRST SENTENCE instructs an agent (as
                       above)                                      [description]
     A mention that is negated ("don't use X", "instead of using X": a
     negation opening its clause within 24 characters), or inside a
     "double-quoted" span, a ``` fence or a > quote, never routes; the first
     remaining mention wins. Description mentions after the first sentence
     never route (pasted briefs and logs live there); they become route
     warnings. A named route-only agent, or a read-only one on an edit task,
     still routes, with a warning.
     fixer / review routes return no skills (the V11 review contract fixes the
     whole brief); an explicit agent still gets scored skills.
  2. The engine returns relevance in [0, 1] per candidate (ENGINES; below).
     Engine "baseline" (BaselineEngine): BM25 (k1=1.2, b=0.75) per field,
     summed with FIELD_WEIGHTS over name + triggers + description + a text
     digest of the file body (the first DIGEST_MAX_LINES non-blank body lines,
     capped at DIGEST_MAX_CHARS). Agents and skills are separate indexes
     (separate IDF). Relevance = BM25 / the query's best BM25.
  3. Shared post-steps (Advisor, identical for every engine; advice.components
     records which of the two optional ones ran):
       filter    drop names in query["exclude"] (ROUTE_ONLY_AGENTS always; on
                 an "edit" task also every agent with neither Edit nor Write),
                 names not in the roster, and duplicates;
       prior     (--no-prior skips it) agents only: build_candidates(meta,
                 complexity) from scripts/agent-recommend (its META_MAP and
                 complexity routing, imported, not copied) adds PRIOR_WEIGHTS
                 by position; recorded as advice.prior;
       tie-break (--no-tiebreak skips it) agents only: exact score ties (4 dp)
                 that touch the top-3 are ordered by the agent-scorecard
                 success rate (agent-recommend.scorecard_lookup), then by name.
  4. Rule tables in this file derive meta, activity, complexity, model, effort
     (META_RULES, ACTIVITY_VERBS, COMPLEXITY_RULES, MODEL_TABLE, EFFORT_TABLE).

Query text: --text is used as-is. For a task, subject terms weigh 1.0 and
description terms DESCRIPTION_QUERY_WEIGHT; the rule tables read the subject
only (a spec-length description would trip every keyword).

advice_id = sha256(engine_tag \\0 roster_hash \\0 task text \\0 canonical JSON
of the metadata the fixed routes read [\\0 the scorecard rates a tie-break
used])[:16], where engine_tag = "<engine>@<version>;rules@<RULES_VERSION>:
<rules fingerprint>;cfg@<config fingerprint>;post@<components on>". The rules
fingerprint hashes the rule tables and route patterns in this file (tests pin
it to RULES_VERSION);
the config fingerprint hashes the engine's ranking constants plus the shared
post-step inputs, including agent-recommend's META_MAP and complexity routing.
So the same text on the same roster through the same configuration always
gets the same id, and any change that can reorder the advice changes it.

Output: one human line per task, or --json for the v2 envelope
(schemas/dispatch-advice.schema.json). Each advice is appended to the side log
~/.agent-metrics/dispatch-advice.jsonl ($METRICS_DIR, or the full path in
$V11_DISPATCH_ADVICE_LOG; "off" disables) under flock as one write, unless
--no-log.

Task selection (S2-T0b-3, #113): a task id is local to one TaskList, and a
resumed session reuses ids, so --task-id matches (session, TaskList epoch, id) on
the aggregate open_tasks. --session defaults to $V11_SESSION_ID, then
$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID; --epoch to the session's epoch record
($METRICS_DIR/tasklist-epochs/<session>), or for a task carried into the
record's epoch the epoch it was created in (review #26). The session's own entries win (a
session holding no open task under the id matches every session's, with a
stderr note naming the session advised); among them an entry stamped with
another TaskList epoch is not the task. More than one match is a real tie: the
matches are listed on stderr and the exit is 2.
--pending never routes a pair_* hook shadow (it counts as a review sibling).
Rollback: V11_TASK_RESOLVER=legacy (a bare id, the best status wins).

Fail-open: a missing roster, task state, task, scorecard or agent-recommend, or
any internal error while advising or rendering, prints "dispatch-advise: no
advice (<reason>)" (status no_advice in --json) and exits 0. A failed log write
is a stderr warning; undecodable text (lone surrogates) is written with
replacement characters. Bad flags exit 2 (argparse).

Environment:
  SESSIONS_ROOT            task-state root (default ~/sessions)
  V11_DISPATCH_ADVICE_LOG  advice log path, or "off"
  METRICS_DIR              directory of the default advice log
  V11_AGENT_SCORECARD      agent-scorecard path, or "off" (no tie-break lookups)
  V11_ROSTER_CACHE         roster cache path (read by roster.py)

Engine interface (how --engine jev plugs in): an engine is built by a factory
in ENGINES, `factory(roster, context) -> engine`, and exposes
    name: str, version: str, config: dict   (JSON-able ranking constants)
    rank_agents(query) -> list[{name, relevance, raw, why}]
    rank_skills(query) -> list[{name, relevance, raw, why}]
where query = {"terms": {stem: weight}, "surface": {stem: word}, "text": str,
"subject": str, "meta": str|None, "complexity": str, "activity": str,
"exclude": set[str]}. relevance is in [0, 1]; raw is the engine's native score
(BM25 for baseline, a probability for Jev) or null. An engine should skip
query["exclude"], and the Advisor drops any it returns anyway. Fixed routes,
the post-steps (filter, prior, tie-break), the rule tables, advice_id, logging
and rendering stay in this file, so two engines differ only in relevance.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
try:
    import fcntl  # POSIX advisory file locking
except ImportError:  # Windows: no fcntl — degrade to no-op advisory locks (single-user; see windows-portability notes)
    class _NoFcntl:
        LOCK_EX = LOCK_SH = LOCK_NB = LOCK_UN = 0
        @staticmethod
        def flock(*_a, **_k):
            return None
    fcntl = _NoFcntl()
import fnmatch
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
import re
import sys
from collections import Counter
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, Callable

SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
LIB_DIR = SCRIPT_DIR / "lib"
AGENT_RECOMMEND = SCRIPT_DIR / "agent-recommend"

ENVELOPE_VERSION = "2"
# Bump when a rule table or route pattern below changes; tests pin
# rules_fingerprint() per RULES_VERSION, so an unbumped edit fails them.
RULES_VERSION = "3"
TOP_K = 3

REVIEWER = "adversarial-lite-reviewer"
FIXER = "adversarial-lite-fixer"
# Reached only through fixed routes (per-task-review.md: the fixer is never a
# general implementer; review siblings are routed by contract).
ROUTE_ONLY_AGENTS = frozenset({REVIEWER, FIXER})
FIX_KINDS = frozenset({"fix", "fixer", "fix-followup", "fix_followup"})
OPEN_STATUSES = ("pending", "in_progress", "blocked")

# --- BM25 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
BM25_K1 = 1.2
BM25_B = 0.75
FIELD_WEIGHTS = {"name": 3.0, "triggers": 2.0, "description": 2.0, "digest": 1.0}
DIGEST_MAX_LINES = 40
DIGEST_MAX_CHARS = 2000
DESCRIPTION_QUERY_WEIGHT = 0.5
DESCRIPTION_QUERY_CHARS = 1500
# Added to the normalised BM25 score of agent-recommend's candidates by position.
PRIOR_WEIGHTS = (0.25, 0.15, 0.10)
MAX_SCORECARD_LOOKUPS = 12  # per process; a larger tie group falls back to name order

STOPWORDS = frozenset(
    "a an the and or but for to of in on at by with from as is are be been was were "
    "this that these those it its into onto via per not no do does did can could "
    "should would will shall may might must i me my we our you your they them their "
    "he she his her so if then than there here what which who whom when where why "
    "how all any each some such only own same too very just also about over under "
    "again further once up down out off new s t don doesn didn isn aren wasn won "
    "shouldn couldn wouldn".split()
)

# A task whose text references the V11 framework itself (an existing repo path
# or a V11 term) is framework work: domain agents are filtered out of its advice
# unless the task names one explicitly. Patterns are fnmatch globs on agent names.
# Paths count only when they resolve inside the repo (parent of scripts/, or
# V11_HOME); generic words like docs/ or a missing docs/x never do.
FRAMEWORK_MARKERS = re.compile(
    r"\bV11\b|\bcontract mode\b|\bwave-check\b|\bsync-tasks\b|\breview-queue\b"
    r"|\bdispatch-advise\b|\bcost-ledger\b|\bTaskUpdate\b",
    re.IGNORECASE)
_PATH_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.\-/])/?\.{0,2}[\w.\-]+(?:/[\w.\-]+)+")
DOMAIN_AGENT_GLOBS = (
    "account-reconciler", "finance-manager", "debt-strategist", "financial-modeler",  # finance/debt
    "herakles-*",  # business development
    "election-*", "dataset-acquirer",  # election
    "example-project-*",
    "stoic-analyst", "morita-analyst", "naikan-analyst", "ubuntu-analyst", "hooponopono-analyst",  # self-reflection
)

# --- Rule tables (documented, tested) ----------------------------------------
# META_RULES: agent-recommend meta-type <- keyword alternation (whole words,
# case-insensitive). The meta with the most distinct matched keywords wins;
# ties go to the earlier row. A task's metadata.meta, when it is a META_MAP key,
# overrides the text.
META_RULES: list[tuple[str, str]] = [
    ("web-app", r"frontend|front-end|react|next\.?js|vue|svelte|ui|ux|css|tailwind|"
                r"web ?page|landing page|components?|dashboards?|website"),
    ("backend-svc", r"api|apis|endpoints?|backend|back-end|fastapi|flask|django|express|"
                    r"server|rest|graphql|database|databases|db|schemas?|sql|postgres(?:ql)?|"
                    r"mongo(?:db)?|redis|quer(?:y|ies)"),
    ("cli-tool", r"cli|command[- ]line|argparse|flags?|subcommands?"),
    ("library", r"library|libraries|sdk|packages?"),
    ("integration", r"integrat\w*|webhooks?|third[- ]party|oauth|connectors?"),
    ("pipeline", r"pipelines?|etl|ingest\w*|batch jobs?|queues?|cron|scheduler"),
    ("realtime", r"websockets?|real[- ]?time|sse|socket\.?io|pub/?sub|live updates?|streaming"),
    ("agent-system", r"agents?|subagents?|skills?|prompts?|orchestrat\w*|mcp|hooks?|routing|router"),
    ("infra", r"docker|compose|nginx|deploy\w*|ci|ci/cd|kubernetes|k8s|containers?|ssl|tls|"
              r"dns|domains?|infra\w*|systemd|cloudflare"),
    ("data-ml", r"ml|machine learning|embeddings?|rag|vectors?|llms?|training|datasets?|inference"),
]

# COMPLEXITY_RULES: first row with a whole-word match wins; nothing -> "medium".
# Values are the task-metadata complexity enum (routine|medium|complex|novel).
COMPLEXITY_RULES: list[tuple[str, str]] = [
    ("novel", r"novel|greenfield|from scratch|spike|prototype|proof of concept|poc|"
              r"research|adr|threat models?|threat modell?ing"),
    ("complex", r"design\w*|architect\w*|schemas?|migrat\w*|security|auth\w*|concurren\w*|"
                r"race conditions?|distributed|redesign\w*|refactor\w*|protocols?|"
                r"multi[- ]service|cross[- ]service|performance|scalab\w*|invariants?"),
    ("routine", r"typos?|renam\w*|bump\w*|format\w*|lint\w*|docs?|readme|comments?|"
                r"changelog|trivial|one[- ]liners?|wording"),
]
DEFAULT_COMPLEXITY = "medium"

# ACTIVITY_VERBS: the task's first word (task codes like "S1-T6:" and "#82"
# skipped) picks the activity when it is a listed verb; otherwise the first
# listed verb anywhere, checked decide > edit > explore; nothing -> "edit".
# Compared after _stem(), so "designing" / "reviews" / "fixed" match.
ACTIVITY_VERBS: dict[str, frozenset[str]] = {
    "decide": frozenset("design architect decide choose plan review audit evaluate assess "
                        "compare triage critique prioritize prioritise scope".split()),
    "edit": frozenset("implement fix add write build create modify refactor update migrate "
                      "delete remove rename deploy configure wire port debug patch bump draft "
                      "generate setup install convert extend make encode re-encode harden".split()),
    "explore": frozenset("find search locate list scan survey inventory grep explore read "
                         "investigate inspect trace check count show probe map diagnose".split()),
}
ACTIVITY_ORDER = ("decide", "edit", "explore")
DEFAULT_ACTIVITY = "edit"

# MODEL_TABLE / EFFORT_TABLE: (activity, complexity) -> tier. Explore reads,
# edit writes, decide judges; effort uses guard-effort's low|medium|high.
COMPLEXITIES = ("routine", "medium", "complex", "novel")
MODEL_TABLE: dict[tuple[str, str], str] = {
    ("explore", "routine"): "haiku",  ("explore", "medium"): "haiku",
    ("explore", "complex"): "sonnet", ("explore", "novel"): "sonnet",
    ("edit", "routine"): "sonnet",    ("edit", "medium"): "sonnet",
    ("edit", "complex"): "opus",      ("edit", "novel"): "opus",
    ("decide", "routine"): "sonnet",  ("decide", "medium"): "opus",
    ("decide", "complex"): "opus",    ("decide", "novel"): "opus",
}
EFFORT_TABLE: dict[tuple[str, str], str] = {
    ("explore", "routine"): "low",    ("explore", "medium"): "low",
    ("explore", "complex"): "medium", ("explore", "novel"): "medium",
    ("edit", "routine"): "low",       ("edit", "medium"): "medium",
    ("edit", "complex"): "high",      ("edit", "novel"): "high",
    ("decide", "routine"): "medium",  ("decide", "medium"): "high",
    ("decide", "complex"): "high",    ("decide", "novel"): "high",
}

_META_RES = [(m, re.compile(rf"\b(?:{rx})\b", re.IGNORECASE)) for m, rx in META_RULES]
_COMPLEXITY_RES = [(c, re.compile(rf"\b(?:{rx})\b", re.IGNORECASE)) for c, rx in COMPLEXITY_RULES]
_REVIEW_TEXT_RE = re.compile(
    r"^\s*review\b\s*(?::|\s+(?:of\s+)?(?:task\s*)?#?\s*[a-z]*\d[\w.-]*)", re.IGNORECASE
)
_FIX_SUBJECT_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:auto-?)?fix(?:er|es|-?up)?\b", re.IGNORECASE)
# Explicit-agent instructions. Weak verbs route only with a trailing "agent" /
# "subagent" ("have the testing-engineer agent fix it"), so "we have
# testing-engineer coverage" does not.
_STRONG_VERBS = (
    r"(?:use|spawn|dispatch(?:\s+to)?|ask|"
    r"(?:delegate|assign|route|hand|send|give)(?:\s+(?:it|this|that))?(?:\s+off)?\s+to)"
)
_WEAK_VERBS = r"(?:using|via|let|have)"
# After the agent name: end of text, punctuation or a closing quote, but not a
# possessive ("use backend-architect's schema" names a thing, not an agent).
_NAME_END = r"(?=$|[\s,.;:!?)\]\"`]|'(?!s\b))"
# A mention is negated when a negation opens its clause no more than 24
# characters before the verb ("don't use X", "instead of using X").
_NEGATION_RE = re.compile(
    r"\b(?:not|never|avoid|without|except|nor|instead\s+of|rather\s+than|no\s+longer|"
    r"don[’']?t|doesn[’']?t|shouldn[’']?t|won[’']?t|can[’']?t)\b[^.;,!?\n]{0,24}$",
    re.IGNORECASE,
)
_FENCE_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*(?:```|~~~)")
_QUOTE_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*>")
_DQ_SPAN_RE = re.compile(r"\"[^\"\n]*\"|“[^”\n]*”")
_SENTENCE_END_RE = re.compile(r"[.!?](?=\s|$)|\n")
# A quoted span at least this long counts as pasted text (brief_has_pasted_text).
PASTED_QUOTE_MIN_CHARS = 60
MAX_ROUTE_WARNINGS = 5
_WORD_RE = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9]+")
_ALPHA_RE = re.compile(r"[a-z]+")


class NoAdvice(Exception):
    """Fail-open exit: the message is the reason printed with 'no advice'."""


class TaskTie(Exception):
    """--task-id names more than one open task: listed on stderr, exit 2."""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Imports that must fail open
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _import_path(name: str, path: Path) -> Any:
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name, str(path))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(name, loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def _load_roster_lib() -> Any:
    sys.path.insert(0, str(LIB_DIR))
    try:
        import roster  # noqa: PLC0415
    finally:
        sys.path.remove(str(LIB_DIR))
    return roster


def _load_agent_recommend() -> tuple[Any | None, str | None]:
    """agent-recommend as a module (META_MAP, build_candidates, scorecard_lookup)."""
    try:
        return _import_path("agent_recommend", AGENT_RECOMMEND), None
    except Exception as e:  # fail-open: no prior, no tie-break
        return None, f"agent-recommend unavailable ({type(e).__name__})"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _stem(w: str) -> str:
    """Tiny deterministic suffix stripper; applied to both query and documents."""
    if len(w) <= 3:
        return w
    if w.endswith("ies") and len(w) > 4:
        w = w[:-3] + "y"
    elif w.endswith(("sses", "xes", "ches", "shes", "zes")):
        w = w[:-2]
    elif w.endswith("s") and not w.endswith(("ss", "us", "is")):
        w = w[:-1]
    elif w.endswith("ing") and len(w) > 5:
        w = w[:-3]
    elif w.endswith("ed") and len(w) > 4:
        w = w[:-2]
    if w.endswith("e") and len(w) > 4:
        w = w[:-1]
    return w


def tokenize(text: str) -> list[str]:
    out = []
    for w in _WORD_RE.findall((text or "").lower()):
        if len(w) < 2 or w.isdigit() or w in STOPWORDS:
            continue
        out.append(_stem(w))
    return out


def _can_edit(entry: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    """True when Edit or Write is in the agent's tool surface."""
    tools = set(entry.get("tools") or ["*"])
    deny = set(entry.get("disallowed_tools") or [])
    return any(("*" in tools or t in tools) and t not in deny for t in ("Edit", "Write"))


def text_digest(path: str | None, split_frontmatter: Callable[[str], tuple[Any, str]]) -> str:
    """First DIGEST_MAX_LINES non-blank body lines of an agent/skill file."""
    if not path:
        return ""
    try:
        text = Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        _, body = split_frontmatter(text)
    except Exception:  # unreadable or malformed: the digest is optional
        return ""
    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in body.splitlines() if ln.strip()][:DIGEST_MAX_LINES]
    return "\n".join(lines)[:DIGEST_MAX_CHARS]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule tables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def infer_meta(text: str, meta_map: dict[str, Any] | None, explicit: Any = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    if meta_map is not None and isinstance(explicit, str) and explicit in meta_map:
        return {"value": explicit, "source": "metadata", "matched": []}
    best: tuple[int, int, str, list[str]] | None = None
    for i, (meta, rx) in enumerate(_META_RES):
        hits = sorted({m.group(0).lower() for m in rx.finditer(text or "")})
        if hits and (best is None or len(hits) > best[0]):
            best = (len(hits), i, meta, hits)
    if best is None:
        return {"value": None, "source": "none", "matched": []}
    return {"value": best[2], "source": "rules", "matched": best[3]}


def infer_complexity(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    for level, rx in _COMPLEXITY_RES:
        hits = sorted({m.group(0).lower() for m in rx.finditer(text or "")})
        if hits:
            return {"value": level, "matched": hits}
    return {"value": DEFAULT_COMPLEXITY, "matched": []}


def _activity_of(word: str) -> str | None:
    s = _stem(word)
    for act in ACTIVITY_ORDER:
        if word in ACTIVITY_VERBS[act] or s in ACTIVITY_VERBS[act]:
            return act
    return None


def infer_activity(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    words = [w for w in _ALPHA_RE.findall((text or "").lower()) if len(w) > 1 and w not in STOPWORDS]
    if words:
        act = _activity_of(words[0])
        if act:
            return {"value": act, "matched": [words[0]], "rule": "leading verb"}
    for act in ACTIVITY_ORDER:
        for w in words:
            if w in ACTIVITY_VERBS[act] or _stem(w) in ACTIVITY_VERBS[act]:
                return {"value": act, "matched": [w], "rule": "keyword"}
    return {"value": DEFAULT_ACTIVITY, "matched": [], "rule": "default"}


def derive(subject: str, meta_map: dict[str, Any] | None, explicit_meta: Any = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    meta = infer_meta(subject, meta_map, explicit_meta)
    complexity = infer_complexity(subject)
    activity = infer_activity(subject)
    key = (activity["value"], complexity["value"])
    return {
        "meta": meta,
        "complexity": complexity,
        "activity": activity,
        "model": MODEL_TABLE[key],
        "effort": EFFORT_TABLE[key],
    }


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixed routes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _truthy(v: Any) -> bool:
    if isinstance(v, str):
        return v.strip().lower() not in ("", "0", "false", "no", "off", "none", "null")
    return bool(v)


def _quoted_spans(text: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
    """Character spans of ``` / ~~~ fences, > quote lines and "double-quoted" text."""
    spans: list[tuple[int, int]] = []
    pos, fence_start = 0, None
    for line in text.splitlines(keepends=True):
        if _FENCE_LINE_RE.match(line):
            if fence_start is None:
                fence_start = pos
            else:
                spans.append((fence_start, pos + len(line)))
                fence_start = None
        elif fence_start is None and _QUOTE_LINE_RE.match(line):
            spans.append((pos, pos + len(line)))
        pos += len(line)
    if fence_start is not None:
        spans.append((fence_start, pos))
    spans.extend((m.start(), m.end()) for m in _DQ_SPAN_RE.finditer(text))
    return spans


def explicit_mentions(text: str, agent_names: list[str]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """Every instruction in text that names a roster agent ("use X", "delegate
    to X", "agent=X", "@X", "have the X agent"), in text order, each with
    negated / quoted flags. Hyphen-less names (Plan, Explore, claude) also need
    a trailing "agent"/"subagent", quotes, "=", ":" or "@" to count."""
    if not text or not agent_names:
        return []
    by_lower = {n.lower(): n for n in agent_names}
    alts = "|".join(re.escape(n) for n in sorted(by_lower, key=lambda n: (-len(n), n)))
    name = rf"(?P<q>[`'\"]?)(?P<name>{alts})(?P=q){_NAME_END}"
    patterns = [
        rf"\b{_STRONG_VERBS}\s+(?:the\s+)?{name}(?P<tail>\s+(?:sub)?agent\b)?",
        rf"\b{_WEAK_VERBS}\s+(?:the\s+)?{name}(?P<tail>\s+(?:sub)?agent\b)",
        rf"(?:\b(?:sub)?agent(?:_type)?\s*[=:]\s*|(?<![\w.])@){name}(?P<tail>)",
    ]
    spans = _quoted_spans(text)
    found: dict[tuple[int, str], dict[str, Any]] = {}
    for p in patterns:
        for m in re.finditer(p, text, re.IGNORECASE):
            agent = by_lower[m.group("name").lower()]
            if "-" not in agent and not (m.group("q") or m.group("tail") or "=" in m.group(0)
                                         or ":" in m.group(0) or "@" in m.group(0)):
                continue
            start = m.start()
            found.setdefault((start, agent), {
                "name": agent,
                "start": start,
                "end": m.end(),
                "text": m.group(0).strip(),
                "negated": bool(_NEGATION_RE.search(text[max(0, start - 80):start])),
                "quoted": any(a < start < b for a, b in spans),
            })
    return [found[k] for k in sorted(found)]


def explicit_agent(text: str, agent_names: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """The first roster agent text instructs, skipping negated and quoted mentions."""
    usable = [m for m in explicit_mentions(text, agent_names) if not m["negated"] and not m["quoted"]]
    return usable[0]["name"] if usable else None


def first_sentence_end(text: str) -> int:
    """End of the first sentence: the first [.!?] before whitespace, or the first newline."""
    m = _SENTENCE_END_RE.search(text or "")
    return m.start() if m else len(text or "")


def has_pasted_text(text: str) -> bool:
    """True when the brief carries pasted material: a ``` / ~~~ fence, a > quote
    line, or a double-quoted span of PASTED_QUOTE_MIN_CHARS or more."""
    for line in (text or "").splitlines():
        if _FENCE_LINE_RE.match(line) or _QUOTE_LINE_RE.match(line):
            return True
    return any(m.end() - m.start() - 2 >= PASTED_QUOTE_MIN_CHARS for m in _DQ_SPAN_RE.finditer(text or ""))


def fixed_route(subject: str, description: str, metadata: dict[str, Any],
                agent_names: list[str]) -> tuple[dict[str, Any] | None, list[str]]:
    """(route or None, warnings). Routes carry kind, agent, rule and provenance:
    review_of (metadata.review_of routes), subject, or description (an
    instruction in the description's first sentence, outside fences/quotes)."""
    warnings: list[str] = []
    review_of = metadata.get("review_of")
    if review_of not in (None, "", []):
        kind = str(metadata.get("kind") or metadata.get("type") or "").strip().lower()
        if _truthy(metadata.get("fix")) or kind in FIX_KINDS or _FIX_SUBJECT_RE.match(subject or ""):
            return {"kind": "fixer", "agent": FIXER, "provenance": "review_of",
                    "rule": f"metadata.review_of={review_of} + fix marker"}, warnings
        return {"kind": "review_sibling", "agent": REVIEWER, "provenance": "review_of",
                "rule": f"metadata.review_of={review_of}"}, warnings

    def pick(mentions: list[dict[str, Any]], where: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
        chosen = None
        for m in mentions:
            if m["negated"] or m["quoted"]:
                why = "negated" if m["negated"] else "quoted"
                warnings.append(f"ignored {why} {where} mention {m['text']!r}")
            elif chosen is None:
                chosen = m
            elif m["name"] != chosen["name"]:
                warnings.append(f"{where} also names {m['name']!r}; routed to the first ({chosen['name']!r})")
        return chosen

    chosen = pick(explicit_mentions(subject, agent_names), "subject")
    if chosen is not None:
        route = {"kind": "explicit_agent", "agent": chosen["name"], "provenance": "subject",
                 "rule": f"subject instructs {chosen['text']!r}"}
    elif (m := _REVIEW_TEXT_RE.match(subject or "")):
        route = {"kind": "review_text", "agent": REVIEWER, "provenance": "subject",
                 "rule": f"subject opens {m.group(0).strip()!r}"}
    else:
        route = None
    cut = first_sentence_end(description)
    described = explicit_mentions(description, agent_names)
    if route is None:
        chosen = pick([m for m in described if m["start"] < cut], "description first-sentence")
        if chosen is not None:
            route = {"kind": "explicit_agent", "agent": chosen["name"], "provenance": "description",
                     "rule": f"description's first sentence instructs {chosen['text']!r}"}
    noted = {route["agent"]} if route else set()
    for m in described:
        if (route is None or m["start"] >= cut) and not (m["negated"] or m["quoted"]) \
                and m["name"] not in noted:
            noted.add(m["name"])
            warnings.append(f"description names {m['name']!r} ({m['text']!r}) after its first sentence; "
                            "not routed: explicit routes come from the subject or the first sentence")
    return route, warnings


def _repo_root() -> Path:
    home = os.environ.get("V11_HOME")
    return (Path(home) if home else SCRIPT_DIR.parent).resolve()


def _names_repo_path(text: str) -> bool:
    root = _repo_root()
    for tok in _PATH_TOKEN_RE.findall(text):
        tok = tok.rstrip(".-")
        p = Path(tok) if tok.startswith("/") else root / tok
        try:
            rel = p.resolve().relative_to(root)
        except (ValueError, OSError):
            continue
        if rel.parts and p.exists():
            return True
    return False


def is_framework_task(text: str) -> bool:
    return bool(FRAMEWORK_MARKERS.search(text)) or _names_repo_path(text)


def domain_agent(name: str) -> bool:
    return any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(name, g) for g in DOMAIN_AGENT_GLOBS)


def rules_fingerprint() -> str:
    """sha256 of every rule table and route pattern in this file."""
    payload = {
        "meta": META_RULES,
        "complexity": [COMPLEXITY_RULES, DEFAULT_COMPLEXITY],
        "activity": [{k: sorted(v) for k, v in ACTIVITY_VERBS.items()}, ACTIVITY_ORDER, DEFAULT_ACTIVITY],
        "model": sorted([*k, v] for k, v in MODEL_TABLE.items()),
        "effort": sorted([*k, v] for k, v in EFFORT_TABLE.items()),
        "routes": [sorted(ROUTE_ONLY_AGENTS), sorted(FIX_KINDS), _REVIEW_TEXT_RE.pattern,
                   _FIX_SUBJECT_RE.pattern, _STRONG_VERBS, _WEAK_VERBS, _NAME_END,
                   _NEGATION_RE.pattern, _FENCE_LINE_RE.pattern, _QUOTE_LINE_RE.pattern,
                   _DQ_SPAN_RE.pattern, _SENTENCE_END_RE.pattern, PASTED_QUOTE_MIN_CHARS,
                   sorted(OPEN_STATUSES)],
        "stopwords": sorted(STOPWORDS),
        "framework": [FRAMEWORK_MARKERS.pattern, FRAMEWORK_MARKERS.flags, list(DOMAIN_AGENT_GLOBS)],
    }
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True).encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Baseline engine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

class BM25Index:
    """Per-field BM25 over roster entries, summed with FIELD_WEIGHTS."""

    def __init__(self, entries: list[dict[str, Any]], split_frontmatter: Callable):
        self.names: list[str] = []
        self.fields: list[dict[str, Counter]] = []
        for e in entries:
            f = {
                "name": Counter(tokenize(re.sub(r"[-_:]", " ", e["name"]))),
                "triggers": Counter(tokenize(" ".join(e.get("triggers") or []))),
                "description": Counter(tokenize(e.get("description") or "")),
                "digest": Counter(tokenize(text_digest(e.get("path"), split_frontmatter))),
            }
            self.names.append(e["name"])
            self.fields.append(f)
        n = len(self.fields)
        self.df: Counter = Counter()
        for f in self.fields:
            self.df.update(set().union(*(c.keys() for c in f.values())))
        self.idf = {t: math.log(1.0 + (n - d + 0.5) / (d + 0.5)) for t, d in self.df.items()}
        self.avglen = {
            k: (sum(sum(f[k].values()) for f in self.fields) / n if n else 0.0) or 1.0
            for k in FIELD_WEIGHTS
        }

    def score(self, terms: dict[str, float]) -> list[tuple[float, dict[str, float]]]:
        out = []
        for f in self.fields:
            total = 0.0
            contrib: dict[str, float] = {}
            for t, qw in terms.items():
                idf = self.idf.get(t)
                if not idf:
                    continue
                s = 0.0
                for k, w in FIELD_WEIGHTS.items():
                    tf = f[k].get(t, 0)
                    if tf:
                        dl = sum(f[k].values())
                        norm = 1 - BM25_B + BM25_B * dl / self.avglen[k]
                        s += w * tf * (BM25_K1 + 1) / (tf + BM25_K1 * norm)
                if s:
                    contrib[t] = idf * s * qw
                    total += contrib[t]
            out.append((total, contrib))
        return out


def _why_terms(contrib: dict[str, float], surface: dict[str, str], limit: int = 3) -> str:
    top = sorted(contrib.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))[:limit]
    return "terms: " + ", ".join(surface.get(t, t) for t, _ in top)


class ScorecardTieBreak:
    """Per-process cache of agent-recommend.scorecard_lookup success rates."""

    def __init__(self, ar_module: Any | None):
        self.lookup = None
        self.state = "unavailable"
        setting = os.environ.get("V11_AGENT_SCORECARD", "")
        if setting.lower() == "off":
            self.state = "disabled"
        elif ar_module is not None:
            if setting:
                ar_module.SCORECARD = Path(setting)
            if Path(ar_module.SCORECARD).exists():
                self.lookup = ar_module.scorecard_lookup
                self.state = "available"
        self.cache: dict[str, float | None] = {}

    def rates(self, names: list[str]) -> dict[str, float | None] | None:
        """Rates for names, or None when unavailable or over the lookup budget."""
        if self.lookup is None:
            return None
        todo = [n for n in names if n not in self.cache]
        if len(self.cache) + len(todo) > MAX_SCORECARD_LOOKUPS:
            return None
        for n in todo:
            try:
                self.cache[n] = self.lookup(n)[0]
            except Exception:
                self.cache[n] = None
        return {n: self.cache[n] for n in names}


class BaselineEngine:
    """Lexical baseline: per-field BM25, relevance = BM25 / the query's best."""

    name = "baseline"
    version = "1.1.0"
    config = {
        "bm25": [BM25_K1, BM25_B], "fields": FIELD_WEIGHTS,
        "digest": [DIGEST_MAX_LINES, DIGEST_MAX_CHARS],
        "description_query": [DESCRIPTION_QUERY_WEIGHT, DESCRIPTION_QUERY_CHARS],
    }

    def __init__(self, roster: dict[str, Any], context: dict[str, Any]):
        split = context["split_frontmatter"]
        self.agents = BM25Index(roster["agents"], split)
        self.skills = BM25Index(roster["skills"], split)

    @staticmethod
    def _rank(index: BM25Index, query: dict[str, Any], exclude: set[str]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
        scored = [(n, s) for n, s in zip(index.names, index.score(query["terms"]))
                  if n not in exclude and s[0] > 0]
        best = max((s[0] for _, s in scored), default=0.0)
        surface = query.get("surface") or {}
        return [{"name": n, "relevance": raw / best, "raw": round(raw, 4),
                 "why": [_why_terms(contrib, surface)]}
                for n, (raw, contrib) in scored]

    def rank_agents(self, query: dict[str, Any]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
        return self._rank(self.agents, query, query.get("exclude") or set())

    def rank_skills(self, query: dict[str, Any]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
        return self._rank(self.skills, query, set())


ENGINES: dict[str, Callable[[dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any]], Any]] = {
    "baseline": BaselineEngine,
}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Task input
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _sessions_root() -> Path:
    env = os.environ.get("SESSIONS_ROOT")
    return Path(env) if env else Path.home() / "sessions"


def load_open_tasks(project: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """open_tasks of ~/sessions/<project>/.task-state.json as a list of
    {task_id, subject, description, status, metadata}; array or object form."""
    if not project or "/" in project or project in (".", ".."):
        raise NoAdvice(f"bad project name {project!r}")
    path = _sessions_root() / project / ".task-state.json"
    try:
        state = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise NoAdvice(f"task state unreadable: {path} ({type(e).__name__})") from None
    raw = state.get("open_tasks") if isinstance(state, dict) else None
    if isinstance(raw, dict):
        items = [({**v, "task_id": str(v.get("task_id") or v.get("id") or k)})
                 for k, v in raw.items() if isinstance(v, dict)]
    elif isinstance(raw, list):
        items = [({**v, "task_id": str(v.get("task_id") or v.get("id") or "")})
                 for v in raw if isinstance(v, dict)]
    else:
        raise NoAdvice(f"no open_tasks in {path}")
    out = []
    for t in items:
        md = t.get("metadata")
        out.append({
            "task_id": t["task_id"],
            "subject": str(t.get("subject") or ""),
            "description": str(t.get("description") or ""),
            "status": str(t.get("status") or ""),
            "metadata": md if isinstance(md, dict) else {},
            "_session": str(t.get("session_uuid") or ""),
            "_tl_epoch": t.get("tl_epoch"),
        })
    return out


def resolver_shared() -> bool:
    return os.environ.get("V11_TASK_RESOLVER", "shared") != "legacy"


def default_session() -> str:
    return os.environ.get("V11_SESSION_ID") or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID") or ""


def record_epoch(session: str, task_id: str | None = None) -> int | None:
    """The session's current TaskList epoch from its record, or None. With a
    task_id, the epoch that task is stamped with: a task carried into the
    current epoch keeps the one it was created in (review #26,
    task_epoch.epoch_for_task)."""
    if not session:
        return None
    sys.path.insert(0, str(LIB_DIR))
    try:
        import task_epoch  # noqa: PLC0415
        rec = task_epoch.read_epoch_record(session)
        if task_id is not None:
            return task_epoch.epoch_for_task(rec, task_id)
    except Exception:
        return None
    finally:
        sys.path.remove(str(LIB_DIR))
    return rec.tl_epoch if rec is not None else None


def _epoch_of(t: dict[str, Any]) -> int | None:
    v = t.get("_tl_epoch")
    if isinstance(v, float) and v.is_integer():
        v = int(v)
    elif isinstance(v, str) and v.isdigit():
        v = int(v)
    return v if isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool) and v > 0 else None


def find_task(tasks: list[dict[str, Any]], task_id: str, session: str = "",
              epoch: int | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    tid = task_id.lstrip("#").strip()
    matches = [t for t in tasks if t["task_id"] == tid]
    if not matches:
        raise NoAdvice(f"task {tid} not in open_tasks")
    if not resolver_shared():
        rank = {"in_progress": 0, "pending": 1, "blocked": 2}
        return sorted(matches, key=lambda t: rank.get(t["status"], 3))[0]
    mine = [t for t in matches if session and t.get("_session") == session]
    if mine:
        if epoch is not None:
            other = sorted({str(_epoch_of(t)) for t in mine})
            mine = [t for t in mine if _epoch_of(t) in (None, epoch)]
            if not mine:
                raise NoAdvice(f"task {tid} of session {session[:8]} is open only in TaskList "
                               f"epoch {', '.join(other)}, not in epoch {epoch}")
        matches = mine
    if len(matches) > 1:
        raise TaskTie(f"task {tid} names {len(matches)} open tasks; pass --session (and --epoch) "
                      "to pick one:\n" + "\n".join(
                          f"  session {t.get('_session') or '?'} epoch {_epoch_of(t) or '-'} "
                          f"[{t['status']}] {t['subject'][:70]}" for t in matches))
    if session and not mine:
        # The named session holds no open task under the id: say whose task
        # this is rather than advise it silently (review #23).
        try:
            print(f"dispatch-advise: note — session {session[:8]} holds no open task {tid}; "
                  f"advising session {(matches[0].get('_session') or '?')[:8]}'s "
                  f"[{matches[0]['status']}] {matches[0]['subject'][:70]}", file=sys.stderr)
        except Exception:
            pass
    return matches[0]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Advice
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _route_metadata(md: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    keys = ("review_of", "fix", "kind", "type", "meta")
    return {k: md[k] for k in keys if k in md and md[k] not in (None, "")}


def advice_id(engine_tag: str, roster_hash: str, text: str, md: dict[str, Any],
              tiebreak_rates: dict[str, float | None] | None = None) -> str:
    parts = [engine_tag, roster_hash, text,
             json.dumps(_route_metadata(md), sort_keys=True, default=str)]
    if tiebreak_rates:
        parts.append(json.dumps(tiebreak_rates, sort_keys=True))
    return hashlib.sha256("\0".join(parts).encode("utf-8", "surrogatepass")).hexdigest()[:16]


def _fingerprint(obj: Any) -> str:
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, default=str).encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()[:12]


def query_terms(subject: str, description: str) -> tuple[dict[str, float], dict[str, str]]:
    """({stem: weight}, {stem: first surface word}); subject terms win."""
    terms: dict[str, float] = {}
    surface: dict[str, str] = {}
    for text, weight in ((description[:DESCRIPTION_QUERY_CHARS], DESCRIPTION_QUERY_WEIGHT), (subject, 1.0)):
        for w in _WORD_RE.findall(text.lower()):
            t = tokenize(w)
            if t:
                terms[t[0]] = weight
                surface.setdefault(t[0], w)
    return dict(sorted(terms.items())), surface


class Advisor:
    def __init__(self, engine_name: str, prior: bool = True, tiebreak: bool = True):
        try:
            roster_lib = _load_roster_lib()
        except Exception as e:
            raise NoAdvice(f"roster library unavailable ({type(e).__name__})") from None
        self.roster = roster_lib.load_roster()
        if not any(a["kind"] == "agent" for a in self.roster["agents"]) and not self.roster["skills"]:
            raise NoAdvice("roster empty (no registry agents or skills under $HOME)")
        self.notes: list[str] = []
        ar, err = _load_agent_recommend()
        if err:
            self.notes.append(err)
        self.ar = ar
        self.components = {"prior": bool(prior), "tiebreak": bool(tiebreak)}
        self.meta_map = getattr(ar, "META_MAP", None) if ar is not None else None
        self.tiebreak = ScorecardTieBreak(ar)
        self.engine = ENGINES[engine_name](self.roster, {
            "split_frontmatter": roster_lib.split_frontmatter,
            "agent_recommend": ar,
        })
        shared = {
            "prior_weights": PRIOR_WEIGHTS, "top_k": TOP_K,
            "agent_recommend": None if ar is None else {
                k: getattr(ar, k, None) for k in ("META_MAP", "COMPLEXITY_ROUTING", "FALLBACK", "ARCHITECT")},
        }
        cfg = _fingerprint({"engine": getattr(self.engine, "config", None), "shared": shared})
        post = "+".join(k for k, on in self.components.items() if on) or "none"
        self.engine_tag = (f"{self.engine.name}@{self.engine.version};"
                           f"rules@{RULES_VERSION}:{rules_fingerprint()[:12]};cfg@{cfg};post@{post}")
        self.agent_names = [a["name"] for a in self.roster["agents"]]
        self.agent_models = {a["name"]: a.get("model") for a in self.roster["agents"]}
        self.skill_models = {s["name"]: s.get("model") for s in self.roster["skills"]}
        self.read_only = {a["name"] for a in self.roster["agents"] if not _can_edit(a)}

    # --- shared post-steps (every engine) -----------------------------------

    def _prior(self, meta: str | None, complexity: str) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[float, str]], dict | None]:
        """agent-recommend build_candidates(meta, complexity) -> PRIOR_WEIGHTS by position."""
        if self.ar is None or not self.components["prior"]:
            return {}, None
        try:
            cands, fallback = self.ar.build_candidates(meta, complexity)
        except Exception:
            return {}, None
        if fallback:
            return {}, None
        label = f"agent-recommend meta={meta or '-'} complexity={complexity}"
        picked = list(cands[: len(PRIOR_WEIGHTS)])
        return ({a: (PRIOR_WEIGHTS[i], f"{label} #{i + 1} (+{PRIOR_WEIGHTS[i]:.2f})")
                 for i, a in enumerate(picked)}, {"label": label, "agents": picked})

    def _finish(self, rows: Any, models: dict[str, Any], exclude: set[str],
                prior: dict[str, tuple[float, str]]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
        """Filter (excluded, unknown, duplicate), add the prior, sort by (-score, name)."""
        kept: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}
        for r in rows or []:
            n = r.get("name") if isinstance(r, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(n, str) or n in exclude or n not in models or n in kept:
                continue
            try:
                rel = min(max(float(r.get("relevance") or 0.0), 0.0), 1.0)
            except (TypeError, ValueError):
                rel = 0.0
            raw = r.get("raw")
            kept[n] = {"relevance": rel, "raw": round(raw, 4) if isinstance(raw, (int, float)) else None,
                       "why": [str(w) for w in (r.get("why") or [])]}
        for n in prior:
            if n in models and n not in exclude:
                kept.setdefault(n, {"relevance": 0.0, "raw": None, "why": []})
        out = []
        for n, r in kept.items():
            p, p_why = prior.get(n, (0.0, ""))
            score = round(r["relevance"] + p, 4)
            if score <= 0:
                continue
            out.append({"name": n, "score": score, "relevance": round(r["relevance"], 4), "raw": r["raw"],
                        "prior": p, "model": models.get(n), "success_rate": None,
                        "why": r["why"] + ([p_why] if p_why else [])})
        out.sort(key=lambda r: (-r["score"], r["name"]))
        return out

    def _tie_break(self, rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> tuple[str, dict[str, float | None]]:
        """Order exact ties touching the top-3 by scorecard success rate, then name
        (name only when the tiebreak component is off: status "disabled")."""
        status, used = "not_needed", {}
        i = 0
        while i < min(TOP_K, len(rows)):
            j = i
            while j + 1 < len(rows) and rows[j + 1]["score"] == rows[i]["score"]:
                j += 1
            if j > i:
                group = rows[i: j + 1]
                rates = self.tiebreak.rates([r["name"] for r in group]) if self.components["tiebreak"] else None
                if rates is None:
                    if status == "not_needed":
                        status = ("disabled" if not self.components["tiebreak"]
                                  else self.tiebreak.state if self.tiebreak.state != "available" else "skipped")
                else:
                    status = "used"
                    for r in group:
                        rate = rates[r["name"]]
                        r["success_rate"] = rate
                        used[r["name"]] = rate
                        r["why"].append(f"tie-break: scorecard {rate:.2f}" if rate is not None
                                        else "tie-break: no scorecard data")
                    group.sort(key=lambda r: (-(r["success_rate"] if r["success_rate"] is not None else -1.0),
                                              r["name"]))
                    rows[i: j + 1] = group
            i = j + 1
        return status, used

    # --- advice ---------------------------------------------------------------

    def advise(self, subject: str, description: str = "", metadata: dict[str, Any] | None = None,
               task: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
        md = metadata or {}
        text = subject if not description else f"{subject}\n{description}"
        derived = derive(subject, self.meta_map, md.get("meta"))
        activity = derived["activity"]["value"]
        route, warnings = fixed_route(subject, description, md, self.agent_names)
        # Agent-naming instructions ("use X", "don't use Y") describe routing, not
        # the work: blank them out of the scoring query.
        scoring_subject = subject
        for m in explicit_mentions(subject, self.agent_names):
            scoring_subject = (scoring_subject[:m["start"]] + " " * (m["end"] - m["start"])
                               + scoring_subject[m["end"]:])
        terms, surface = query_terms(scoring_subject, description)
        exclude = set(ROUTE_ONLY_AGENTS) | (self.read_only if activity == "edit" else set())
        base_exclude = frozenset(exclude)
        framework = is_framework_task(text)
        if framework:
            exclude |= {n for n in self.agent_names if domain_agent(n)}
        query = {
            "terms": terms,
            "surface": surface,
            "text": text,
            "subject": subject,
            "meta": derived["meta"]["value"],
            "complexity": derived["complexity"]["value"],
            "activity": activity,
            "exclude": base_exclude,  # domain filter for framework tasks is applied in _finish
        }
        scorecard, rates_used, prior_block = "not_needed", {}, None
        if route is None:
            prior, prior_block = self._prior(query["meta"], query["complexity"])
            rows = self.engine.rank_agents(query)
            agents = self._finish(rows, self.agent_models, exclude, prior)
            scorecard, rates_used = self._tie_break(agents)
            agents = agents[:TOP_K]
            if framework:
                unfiltered = self._finish(rows, self.agent_models, set(base_exclude), prior)[:TOP_K]
                dropped = [r["name"] for r in unfiltered if domain_agent(r["name"])]
                if dropped:
                    warnings.append("framework task: filtered domain agent(s) " + ", ".join(dropped))
            if agents:
                route = {"kind": "scored", "agent": agents[0]["name"], "provenance": "engine",
                         "rule": "engine rank + shared post-steps"}
            else:
                fb = next((n for n in ("spec-implementer-v11", "general-purpose", "claude")
                           if n in self.agent_models and n not in exclude), None)
                route = {"kind": "fallback", "agent": fb, "provenance": "engine",
                         "rule": "no relevance or prior"}
                agents = [] if fb is None else [{
                    "name": fb, "score": 0.0, "relevance": 0.0, "raw": None, "prior": 0.0,
                    "model": self.agent_models.get(fb), "success_rate": None,
                    "why": ["fallback: nothing scored"]}]
        else:
            named = route["agent"]
            if route["kind"] == "explicit_agent":
                if named in ROUTE_ONLY_AGENTS:
                    warnings.append(f"{named!r} is route-only (reserved for review/fix siblings)")
                if activity == "edit" and named in self.read_only:
                    warnings.append(f"{named!r} has neither Edit nor Write but the task reads as an edit")
            agents = [{"name": named, "score": None, "relevance": None, "raw": None, "prior": None,
                       "model": self.agent_models.get(named), "success_rate": None,
                       "why": [f"fixed route {route['kind']}: {route['rule']}"]}]
        route["warnings"] = warnings[:MAX_ROUTE_WARNINGS]
        skills = [] if route["kind"] in ("fixer", "review_sibling", "review_text") \
            else self._finish(self.engine.rank_skills(query), self.skill_models, set(), {})[:TOP_K]
        task_block = {
            "source": "task" if task else "text",
            "project": task.get("project") if task else None,
            "task_id": task.get("task_id") if task else None,
            "status": task.get("status") if task else None,
            "subject": subject,
            "tagged": ({k: (str(md[k]) if md.get(k) not in (None, "") else None)
                        for k in ("agent", "complexity", "scope")} if task else None),
        }
        return {
            "advice_id": advice_id(self.engine_tag, self.roster["roster_hash"], text, md, rates_used),
            "task": task_block,
            "route": route,
            "agents": agents,
            "skills": skills,
            "derived": derived,
            "brief_has_pasted_text": has_pasted_text(text),
            "components": dict(self.components),
            "prior": prior_block,
            "scorecard": scorecard,
        }


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _now() -> str:
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds")


def _cands(rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> str:
    if not rows:
        return "-"
    parts = []
    for r in rows:
        s = f"{r['name']}" + (f" {r['score']:.2f}" if r.get("score") is not None else "")
        terms = next((w[len("terms: "):] for w in r["why"] if w.startswith("terms: ")), "")
        extra = [terms] if terms else []
        if r.get("prior"):
            extra.append(f"prior+{r['prior']:.2f}")
        if r.get("success_rate") is not None:
            extra.append(f"sc {r['success_rate']:.2f}")
        parts.append(s + (f" ({'; '.join(extra)})" if extra else ""))
    return " · ".join(parts)


def render_line(a: dict[str, Any], with_task: bool = False) -> str:
    d = a["derived"]
    route = a["route"]
    if route["kind"] in ("scored", "fallback"):
        agents = _cands(a["agents"])
    else:
        agents = f"{route['agent']} [fixed {route['kind']}: {route['rule']}]"
    head = f"adv {a['advice_id']}"
    if with_task:
        t = a["task"]
        tagged = (t.get("tagged") or {}).get("agent") or "-"
        head = f"#{t['task_id']} {t['status']} tagged={tagged} | {head}"
    warn = f" | warnings: {'; '.join(route['warnings'])}" if route.get("warnings") else ""
    return (f"{head} | agents: {agents} | skills: {_cands(a['skills'])} | "
            f"{d['complexity']['value']}/{d['model']}/{d['effort']} "
            f"(activity={d['activity']['value']}, meta={d['meta']['value'] or '-'}){warn}")


def envelope(advisor: Advisor | None, mode: str, advice: list[dict[str, Any]],
             status: str = "ok", reason: str | None = None,
             extra: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    eng = advisor.engine if advisor else None
    return {
        "version": ENVELOPE_VERSION,
        "status": status,
        "reason": reason,
        "generated_at": _now(),
        "mode": mode,
        "engine": {"name": eng.name if eng else None, "version": eng.version if eng else None,
                   "rules_version": RULES_VERSION, "tag": advisor.engine_tag if advisor else None},
        "roster_hash": advisor.roster["roster_hash"] if advisor else None,
        "notes": list(advisor.notes) if advisor else [],
        "advice": advice,
        **({"pending": extra} if extra is not None else {}),
    }


def _log_path() -> Path | None:
    env = os.environ.get("V11_DISPATCH_ADVICE_LOG", "")
    if env.lower() == "off":
        return None
    if env:
        return Path(env)
    metrics = os.environ.get("METRICS_DIR")
    return (Path(metrics) if metrics else Path.home() / ".agent-metrics") / "dispatch-advice.jsonl"


def log_record(advisor: Advisor, a: dict[str, Any], ts: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    t = a["task"]
    return {
        "v": ENVELOPE_VERSION,
        "ts": ts,
        "advice_id": a["advice_id"],
        "engine": advisor.engine.name,
        "engine_version": advisor.engine.version,
        "rules_version": RULES_VERSION,
        "engine_tag": advisor.engine_tag,
        "roster_hash": advisor.roster["roster_hash"],
        "source": t["source"],
        "project": t["project"],
        "task_id": t["task_id"],
        "subject": t["subject"][:200],
        "tagged_agent": (t.get("tagged") or {}).get("agent"),
        "route": a["route"]["kind"],
        "route_provenance": a["route"]["provenance"],
        "brief_has_pasted_text": a["brief_has_pasted_text"],
        "components": a["components"],
        "agents": [{"name": r["name"], "score": r["score"]} for r in a["agents"]],
        "skills": [{"name": r["name"], "score": r["score"]} for r in a["skills"]],
        "complexity": a["derived"]["complexity"]["value"],
        "model": a["derived"]["model"],
        "effort": a["derived"]["effort"],
    }


def append_log(path: Path, records: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> None:
    """All records in one write under an exclusive flock (O_APPEND)."""
    if not records:
        return
    data = "".join(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n" for r in records)
    payload = data.encode("utf-8", "replace")  # a lone surrogate becomes "?", never a crash
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(str(path), os.O_WRONLY | os.O_APPEND | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        try:
            os.write(fd, payload)
        finally:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _run(args: argparse.Namespace) -> tuple[Advisor, str, list[dict[str, Any]], dict[str, Any] | None]:
    if args.text is not None:
        if not args.text.strip():
            raise NoAdvice("empty --text")
        advisor = Advisor(args.engine, prior=not args.no_prior, tiebreak=not args.no_tiebreak)
        return advisor, "text", [advisor.advise(args.text.strip())], None
    if args.task_id is not None:
        if not args.project:
            raise NoAdvice("--task-id needs --project")
        session = default_session() if args.session is None else args.session
        epoch = (args.epoch if args.epoch is not None
                 else record_epoch(session, args.task_id.lstrip("#").strip()))
        t = find_task(load_open_tasks(args.project), args.task_id, session, epoch)
        advisor = Advisor(args.engine, prior=not args.no_prior, tiebreak=not args.no_tiebreak)
        t["project"] = args.project
        return advisor, "task", [advisor.advise(t["subject"], t["description"], t["metadata"], t)], None
    tasks = load_open_tasks(args.pending)
    work, reviews, fixers = [], [], []
    for t in tasks:
        if t["status"] not in OPEN_STATUSES:
            continue
        if resolver_shared() and t["task_id"].startswith("pair_"):
            reviews.append(t)  # a hook review shadow, never TaskList work (S2-T0b-3)
            continue
        if t["metadata"].get("review_of") in (None, "", []):
            work.append(t)
            continue
        route, _ = fixed_route(t["subject"], "", t["metadata"], [])
        (fixers if route["kind"] == "fixer" else reviews).append(t)
    advisor = Advisor(args.engine, prior=not args.no_prior, tiebreak=not args.no_tiebreak)
    out = []
    for t in work:
        t["project"] = args.pending
        out.append(advisor.advise(t["subject"], t["description"], t["metadata"], t))
    extra = {"project": args.pending, "open_work_tasks": len(work),
             "review_siblings_skipped": len(reviews), "fixer_tasks_skipped": len(fixers)}
    return advisor, "pending", out, extra


def _render(args: argparse.Namespace, mode_name: str, env: dict[str, Any], advisor: Advisor,
            advice: list[dict[str, Any]], extra: dict[str, Any] | None) -> str:
    if args.json:
        return json.dumps(env, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    lines = []
    if mode_name == "pending":
        lines.append(
            f"dispatch-advise --pending {extra['project']} [{advisor.engine.name} "
            f"{advisor.engine.version} · roster {advisor.roster['roster_hash'][:8]} · "
            f"{extra['open_work_tasks']} open work tasks · "
            f"{extra['review_siblings_skipped']} review siblings skipped (fixed route {REVIEWER}) · "
            f"{extra['fixer_tasks_skipped']} fixer tasks skipped (fixed route {FIXER})]")
    lines.extend(render_line(a, with_task=mode_name == "pending") for a in advice)
    return "".join(ln + "\n" for ln in lines)


def _emit(text: str) -> None:
    try:
        sys.stdout.write(text)
        sys.stdout.flush()
    except Exception:  # a closed or unencodable stdout must not turn into exit 1
        pass


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    for stream in (sys.stdout, sys.stderr):
        try:
            stream.reconfigure(errors="replace")
        except (AttributeError, ValueError):
            pass
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Advisory agent + skill router over the live roster (ticket #88). "
                    "Read-only except for the side log; fail-open.")
    mode = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    mode.add_argument("--text", help="free-text task to route")
    mode.add_argument("--task-id", help="route this open task (needs --project)")
    mode.add_argument("--pending", metavar="PROJECT", help="route every open work task of PROJECT")
    ap.add_argument("--project", help="project for --task-id (~/sessions/PROJECT/.task-state.json)")
    ap.add_argument("--session", default=None,
                    help="session of --task-id (default $V11_SESSION_ID, then $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID)")
    ap.add_argument("--epoch", type=int, default=None,
                    help="TaskList epoch of --task-id (default: the session's epoch record)")
    ap.add_argument("--engine", choices=sorted(ENGINES), default="baseline")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print the v2 JSON envelope")
    ap.add_argument("--no-log", action="store_true", help="do not append to dispatch-advice.jsonl")
    ap.add_argument("--no-prior", action="store_true",
                    help="skip the shared agent-recommend META_MAP/complexity prior (rank by engine relevance)")
    ap.add_argument("--no-tiebreak", action="store_true",
                    help="skip the shared agent-scorecard tie-break (exact ties go by name)")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    mode_name = "text" if args.text is not None else "task" if args.task_id is not None else "pending"

    advisor: Advisor | None = None
    try:
        advisor, mode_name, advice, extra = _run(args)
        env = envelope(advisor, mode_name, advice, extra=extra)
        out = _render(args, mode_name, env, advisor, advice, extra)
    except NoAdvice as e:
        return _no_advice(args, mode_name, str(e), advisor)
    except TaskTie as e:
        try:
            print(f"dispatch-advise: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        except Exception:
            pass
        return 2
    except Exception as e:  # fail-open: advice must never break the caller
        return _no_advice(args, mode_name, f"internal error: {type(e).__name__}: {e}", advisor)

    if not args.no_log and advice:
        try:
            path = _log_path()
            if path is not None:
                append_log(path, [log_record(advisor, a, env["generated_at"]) for a in advice])
        except Exception as e:  # the log is a side channel: warn, keep the advice
            try:
                print(f"dispatch-advise: advice log not written ({type(e).__name__}: {e})", file=sys.stderr)
            except Exception:
                pass
    _emit(out)
    return 0


def _no_advice(args: argparse.Namespace, mode_name: str, reason: str, advisor: Advisor | None) -> int:
    try:
        if args.json:
            text = json.dumps(envelope(advisor, mode_name, [], status="no_advice", reason=reason), indent=2)
        else:
            text = f"dispatch-advise: no advice ({reason})"
    except Exception as e:
        text = f"dispatch-advise: no advice (internal error: {type(e).__name__})"
    _emit(text + "\n")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
